# Shadow operators in user scope; prelude functions must still work correctly
# because they use $builtin-lt, $builtin-add, etc. internally.
# $> (prelude) uses $builtin-lt, so shadowing < should not affect it.
[
  <: [fn [a b] false]
  +: [fn [a b] 0]
  gt-result: [> 5 3]
  not-result: [not false]
]
=== out
Dict({"<": Function(a, b), "+": Function(a, b), "gt-result": Bool(true), "not-result": Bool(true)})
=== warn
undefined variable: > at 6:15-6:16
undefined variable: not at 7:16-7:19
